radical and you know,

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:30.780
but I just, I don't agree

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:34.980
with the whole transgender ideology.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:38.220
And so for me it's encouraging something

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:41.220
that is based in what I feel is delusion.

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:44.340
And so I don't think that
we should be encouraging

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:49.143
that by allowing men
into women's restrooms.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:55.380
- I think that if that's the case,

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:59.490
that to some extent
all gender is delusion.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:04.470
If we're looking at
historically anywhere from,

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:07.050
you know, midwives after the enclosure

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:09.003
of the Commons in the 1400s,

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:13.200
having their whole trade affected

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.390
or brewsters having their trade affected.

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:17.070
And now we don't think
of women as, you know,

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:20.913
brewsters or that creating
beer is a womanly thing.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:23.700
These all came from social conditions.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:24.840
These all came,

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.990
a lot of gender regardless
of biological sex,

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.240
it didn't like naturally
flow out of our genitals.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:31.890
And like, it was like,
you know, we're like,

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:33.960
this is how my genitals are,

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.180
so this is like how my gender's gonna be.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:37.013
That didn't happen.

00:11:37.013 --> 00:11:38.250
That's not life.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.680
Like a lot of people who
are either transgender

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:43.200
or who are LGBT in general,

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.520
all my friends were girls.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:46.920
At first, I just remember
there were a lot of things

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:48.750
where like, I would kind of like come up

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.690
against people telling
me that that's wrong.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.570
Like that, whether it's something I like,

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:56.250
something I want to do.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:58.530
It wasn't until kindergarten
that like someone

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:02.522
told me that I'm a boy and I was like, oh.

00:12:02.522 --> 00:12:06.346
I don't feel comfortable
going to any bathroom

00:12:06.346 --> 00:12:08.130
in this world.

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:09.990
Like in the current society we live in,

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:13.361
and to make trans women
the whipping girls of that,

00:12:13.361 --> 00:12:15.450
I think that's disingenuous.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:18.180
But I do think that we
need a systemic change

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:20.280
to make ourselves safer.

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.410
I don't really know anyone who doesn't

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:25.260
feel a little bit uncomfortable
going to the bathroom.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.060
- And trans people are not a delusion.

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:28.410
Let's make it very clear.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:29.310
We are here,

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.960
we've been here for ages,

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:32.880
we've been here since
the beginning of time.

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:34.530
We're in your history books.

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:35.730
And I don't think,

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.110
I think it's very disingenuous

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:40.470
to say that a whole
identity is a delusion.

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:42.930
- Well, I believe that
you feel like women.

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:43.950
That's not what I'm saying.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.480
I'm saying there is an objective truth

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:47.340
and I don't believe in
his truth, her truth,

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:48.630
their truth, my truth.

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.760
Like there is truth. And--

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:52.197
- Who defined that truth?

00:12:52.197 --> 00:12:54.750
- And like it's already,
it's already defined.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:55.830
And I, as a Christian,

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.590
I believe God is the one who set truth.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:12:59.880
- But who defined that?

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.920
Can you tell me who defined that?

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:02.777
- God.

00:13:02.777 --> 00:13:03.610
Living in the Bible belt

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:06.360
with religion taking center stage,

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.680
it's hard for a lot of trans

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.420
and non-binary folks like myself

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:11.550
to really be able to express who they are.

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:14.700
I had to really take on my
gender dysphoria in private.

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:16.200
I couldn't talk to my mom about it.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:18.270
I couldn't talk to my dad, my siblings,

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:21.510
because ultimately I felt
like it wasn't gonna lead

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:24.240
to anything because there
wasn't a lot of education

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:26.370
in the cis community like there is

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:28.290
in the trans and non-binary community.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:31.800
We're talking about a book
that was written by man

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:33.810
with his own bias.

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:34.830
- Who created chromosomes?

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.360
- Yeah, I'm personally not religious

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:37.560
and I believe in science.

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:39.180
- When we talk about chromosomes,

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:40.800
it goes back to the
conversation we were talking

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:42.480
about earlier about being intersex.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:43.620
- But we're not talking about intersex.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:46.170
We're talking about people
who were born as a male

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.790
and they tried to transition.

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:49.350
The whole fact that they're
trying to transition

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:50.820
into a female in the first place shows

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:53.160
that they aren't actually that that

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:54.920
or else there would be no
need to transition, right?

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:56.370
So you say, okay, I feel like a woman.

00:13:56.370 --> 00:13:57.660
What is that? What does that feel like?

00:13:57.660 --> 00:13:58.950
- Yeah, how does that feel?
- And how do you know?

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.020
- We're not saying, I'm not
saying I feel like a woman.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.160
I am a woman.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.540
- So, then why did you transition?

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:06.480
Why can't you just present
as a man but be a woman?

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:08.790
- I transitioned so I could be who I was.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:10.740
I did not feel like I was the person

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.870
that I identified with when I was born.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.380
So, I took the steps to
align my outside body

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.030
with how I feel on the inside.

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:20.280
What makes you stand up
every day and make you

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:21.210
identify as a woman?

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:22.290
Let me challenge you on that.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.630
- I am a woman and I don't
like being called a cis woman,

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.463
because I'm not a cis woman.

00:14:25.463 --> 00:14:26.370
I'm a woman.

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:27.540
I'm not a birthing person.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:28.373
I'm a mother.

00:14:28.373 --> 00:14:29.790
- So, get mad at the terminology,

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:30.623
not at trans people.

00:14:30.623 --> 00:14:32.370
- It's your new terminology.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:33.203
- But this is what,

00:14:33.203 --> 00:14:36.540
this is what I notice
a lot of cis women do.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:38.880
The terminology has
been around for so long.

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.440
Cis is a prefix.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.693
Cis means same.

00:14:41.693 --> 00:14:44.850
Instead of getting mad at
trans and non-binary people

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:47.010
for using updated terminology,

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:48.510
get mad at Webster.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:51.030
You're not going along with
the times and being educated

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:55.230
on the different pronouns
and the different identities.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:56.370
- You have to admit some of the pronouns

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:57.816
are kind of ridiculous.

00:14:57.816 --> 00:14:59.040
I mean the,

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.090
to be with all due respect,

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:00.923
I mean, I mean you, you,

00:15:00.923 --> 00:15:02.850
I'm sure you have to agree
some of the pronouns--

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:04.200
- I don't think they're ridiculous.

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:06.060
I think they're very expansive,

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:07.140
trans and non-binary.

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:09.810
People just want you to
respect they're chosen pronoun.

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:12.480
We are not trying to
force pronouns on you.

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:14.580
Just understanding that the terminology

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.230
is going to continue to grow.

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:19.710
If you're willing to educate
yourself and understand,

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:20.910
then you've got it.

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:23.100
- [Narrator] The ability to give birth

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:25.443
is a woman's greatest strength.

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:32.050
Can the disagreers or step forward?

00:15:40.906 --> 00:15:43.200
- I'm not able to have children.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.910
So, I'm still strong.

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.227
I'm funny, I'm physically strong.

00:15:47.227 --> 00:15:49.770
I'm smart and I have a lot of strength.

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:51.570
I don't believe that having a baby

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:52.950
is the greatest strength,

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:54.420
'cause not all of us can,

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:57.630
I cannot have kids due to medical issues

00:15:57.630 --> 00:16:01.383
from a medical procedure that
I had when I was younger.

00:16:02.794 --> 00:16:07.794
And it's a hard subject to talk about.

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:11.760
It's doesn't mean, I
mean, I'm less of a woman,

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:14.940
but can we get another question?

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:17.130
I don't, yeah, I'm sorry.

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.720
It's, it's, I'm sorry.

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:20.010
- One of the things that I regret

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:22.530
was the fact that I would
never be able to do that,

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:26.430
but I was honored and the
ability to participate it

00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:27.960
from the other side.

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:29.430
Women are amazing.

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:32.190
They don't just deal with that, so.

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:34.470
- While giving birth is not
a woman's greatest strength,

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.570
I do think that only biological women

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:39.480
are capable of going through that process,

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:41.310
and bringing life into the world.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:42.450
- I need to push back on that,

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:44.640
because we're also
forgetting that trans men

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:47.670
and trans masculine people
can also give birth as well.

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:50.760
And I don't think it's fair
to just set it on one group

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:52.980
that says it just biological women

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:54.960
have that power to just give birth.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:57.210
And we have to be very clear

00:16:57.210 --> 00:17:00.240
when we look at the nuances of birth.

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:01.530
- I recognize that there are people

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:02.760
who have different identities.

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:06.390
There are a biological
women who identify as men

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:09.450
and then go on to give birth.

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:10.710
I would argue however,

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:13.860
that those people are
still biological women.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.230
And I know that is something
that can offend many,

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:18.270
but that stands as my belief.

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:21.120
- So, the correct term is
actually cisgendered woman.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:22.140
Cis means same.

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:24.180
It means that you identify with the birth

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.740
that you were assigned.

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:29.040
And so, you know, I
just really. really wish

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.710
that we would kind of be
a little bit more mutable

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:33.570
to the terminology,

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.550
because I think that's what
really is gonna open up

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:37.620
that dialogue and that discussion.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:38.453
- If I may,

00:17:38.453 --> 00:17:39.870
I think the crux of the conversation kind

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:43.350
of comes back to are trans women, women?

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:45.690
And I think if we don't agree there,

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:46.800
it's gonna be very difficult

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:49.012
to kind of keep the conversation going

00:17:49.012 --> 00:17:52.200
or even agree on the points
that you guys are talking about.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:56.430
Because if we don't believe
that trans women are women,

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:59.460
then the conversation kind of ends there,

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:01.830
in terms of whether they're,

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:05.070
like men can give birth or
not, if that makes sense.

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:06.600
- I'm not sure that's the case.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:09.570
I feel like the ability to give birth

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:11.880
is not like the end all, be all

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.370
of a woman's like meaning and life

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:18.540
and herself and her personality.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:21.270
And I think that if you
can acknowledge that,

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:24.780
I would also then maybe challenge the idea

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:29.490
that womanhood, as opposed
to like a female sex,

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:33.000
like womanhood is a consistent thing

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.940
that has always been one way.

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:37.833
- So, how would you define womanhood?

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:40.413
- You sound like Matt Walsh.

00:18:40.413 --> 00:18:42.240
(laughter)

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:43.140
- It's a good question.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:48.000
- Womanhood to me is about
standing in integrity.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:50.580
It is about being
confident in who you are.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:55.080
And me as a black trans woman
should not be a threat to you.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:57.480
And what I see from a
lot of cisgender women

00:18:57.480 --> 00:18:59.970
is they're trying to deem what womanhood

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:01.350
is supposed to look like.

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:03.930
I have my own perspective of womanhood.

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:07.020
We can coexist in the same world,

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:10.620
but the reality is we
get so stuck on parts.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:13.920
Having a vagina is not the only thing

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.390
that makes you a woman.

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:16.590
I'm sorry.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:19.260
It takes integrity, it takes courage,

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.750
it takes lifting other women up.

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:24.960
It takes those things to
begin to defy womanhood

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:26.790
and there's so many
other different things.

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:28.260
- Can I ask you a question?

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:29.414
- Sure.

00:19:29.414 --> 00:19:30.960
- Okay, so if I were a white person

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:34.860
and I said blackness is
about integrity and courage

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:36.210
and kind of the same thing that you've

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:37.590
used to define womanhood.

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:42.590
And then I said, I wanna
transition into a black person

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:46.140
and I'm white and I'm
redefining what blackness

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:48.240
is to fit what I view it as, right?

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:51.300
There's no objective reality
of what blackness is.

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:53.130
Would you consider that appropriation

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:55.500
or do you think that's something
I should be allowed to do?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:56.850
- I consider that dodging,

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:59.250
and I consider that
comparing apples to oranges,

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:00.750
because race and gender identity

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:02.460
are two, separate different things,

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:04.050
because when we look at race,

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:06.900
we have to look at many,
many different structures

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:09.600
of what whiteness and
white supremacy looks like

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.910
and how white supremacy can be manipulated

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:13.140
into other things.

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:15.390
And what happens is the closer you are

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:17.460
in proximity to whiteness,

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:20.040
you're able to weaponize
it against other people.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:23.310
It reminds me a lot of
Rachel Dolezal who, you know,

00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:25.770
masqueraded as a black woman.

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:27.390
It really did open up many more doors

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:28.800
of conversations around it.

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:30.630
But it's still wrong,

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:33.150
it's still not fair because
she was still ultimately

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:35.430
have a privilege that I
as a black trans woman

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:37.114
would not begin to have.

00:20:37.114 --> 00:20:38.880
- What's interesting is that we are,

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:41.640
we're talking about race and gender

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:44.460
or as we probably like to
call it on our side, sex.

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:47.460
Race actually has a more
understandable structure

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:49.170
for people being transracial.

00:20:49.170 --> 00:20:51.510
Race does actually exist on a spectrum.

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:52.650
I'm biracial.

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:54.360
Many perceive me to be black,

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:57.180
even though I am also
half white and half black.

00:20:57.180 --> 00:20:59.790
We label people like President
Obama as a black president,

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:01.320
even though he is as well.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.120
Race is never had binary markers.

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:04.860
It does exist on a spectrum.

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:07.980
Gender, however, does have binary markers.

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:09.090
As much as we try,

00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:12.064
as much as we change the
way that we self present,

00:21:12.064 --> 00:21:14.662
chromosomes are not going to change.

00:21:14.662 --> 00:21:15.495
- Okay.

00:21:15.495 --> 00:21:17.040
- And that's just a reality.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.034
- All right.

00:21:18.034 --> 00:21:19.410
I'm gonna bring up a little
point here because you

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:22.353
talked about the binary side of gender.

00:21:22.353 --> 00:21:24.243
Well, I was born a little both.

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:26.490
I believe my,

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:28.050
I've never had my chromosomes checked,

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:30.510
but since I had, I fathered two children,

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:33.480
I'm assuming I have the
correct male of chromosomes.

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:36.090
So, I was intersexed and
there's a lot of reasons

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:37.530
that that happens,

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:39.660
none of which are
well-studied or understood.

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:43.140
But a friend of mine in
the pediatric trauma world

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:46.080
says about one in 150 kids
come out with some degree

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.790
of ambiguity in their gender.

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:52.790
For me that that appeared as
always feeling outta place.

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:55.500
And I'm, for the first week of my life,

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:59.125
I was in the surgical wards at, you know,

00:21:59.125 --> 00:22:03.060
Naval Hospital in San Diego
getting pieces of me cut off.

00:22:03.060 --> 00:22:04.830
So, and then they gave me testosterone

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:06.870
for the first 11 years of my life.

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:11.870
I wish the world were
truly sexually binary.

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:15.150
It would make it so much easier.

00:22:15.150 --> 00:22:17.490
But there is a little bit
of a smear and you know,

00:22:17.490 --> 00:22:20.476
as a trans person, I'm a very
conservative trans person.

00:22:20.476 --> 00:22:25.040
I don't see the huge gender spectrum

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:28.350
that a lot of people in
the trans community do.

00:22:28.350 --> 00:22:30.510
Do I feel better having transitioned?

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:31.800
Yes, absolutely.

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:34.390
I used to live in a little shell,

00:22:34.390 --> 00:22:36.120
well, very large shell,

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:38.439
but, you know, but you know,

00:22:38.439 --> 00:22:39.910
now I'm, you know,

00:22:39.910 --> 00:22:43.020
much more open about who I am, you know?

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:46.050
Is that the only thing that
generally defines a woman?

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:48.360
No, I don't think that is the only thing

00:22:48.360 --> 00:22:49.800
that generally defines woman.

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:53.250
- Right, I think there
are a lot of women who may

00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:55.380
be on our side of the
argument who will try

00:22:55.380 --> 00:22:57.570
to maybe invalidate your experiences

00:22:57.570 --> 00:22:59.280
by saying you can't give birth

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:00.960
or you can't have a period.

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:02.400
And while those things may be true,

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:04.560
I'm sure there's a lot of
other different struggles

00:23:04.560 --> 00:23:07.188
that you all are going through and yeah,

00:23:07.188 --> 00:23:11.220
I would truly believe that you probably

00:23:11.220 --> 00:23:14.520
are highly discriminated
against in our society.

00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:16.890
And it is hard to be you.

00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:18.900
It is hard to go through the
things that you go through

00:23:18.900 --> 00:23:20.310
and have to deal with
some of the responses

00:23:20.310 --> 00:23:21.270
that you get from people.

00:23:21.270 --> 00:23:23.730
And, you know, it's not a
struggle that I would wish

00:23:23.730 --> 00:23:24.563
on myself at all.

00:23:24.563 --> 00:23:27.540
- Not a struggle I wish on my worst enemy.

00:23:27.540 --> 00:23:29.520
- [Narrator] Trans women should be allowed

00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:31.683
to compete in women's sports.

00:23:35.263 --> 00:23:37.380
- I do think that trans
women have every right

00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:38.970
to compete in women's sports.

00:23:38.970 --> 00:23:40.680
When trans women are on hormones,

00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:42.840
the hormones break their body down.

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:44.520
Having gender affirming surgery

00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:45.720
breaks down down the body.

00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:48.115
And so I think we really
need to be educated

00:23:48.115 --> 00:23:51.660
before we jump to a
conclusion that trans women

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:53.703
are stronger than cis women in sports.

00:23:56.010 --> 00:23:56.973
Hi, everybody.

00:23:57.825 --> 00:24:01.500
- I find it interesting
that you assume the people

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:03.840
who disagree with you are uneducated.

00:24:03.840 --> 00:24:06.420
And I will speak out against that.

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:08.940
I think the research
shows that trans women

00:24:08.940 --> 00:24:11.142
do happen to have a biological advantage

00:24:11.142 --> 00:24:13.650
against biological women.

00:24:13.650 --> 00:24:15.060
Even though you are taking hormones

00:24:15.060 --> 00:24:16.530
and that does start to change your body

00:24:16.530 --> 00:24:17.820
and level things out,

00:24:17.820 --> 00:24:20.070
we are talking about primarily people

00:24:20.070 --> 00:24:21.990
who have transitioned post-puberty,

00:24:21.990 --> 00:24:24.210
which means they do
have male bone density,

00:24:24.210 --> 00:24:26.460
male wingspan, male hand size,

00:24:26.460 --> 00:24:28.380
feet size, lung capacity.

00:24:28.380 --> 00:24:30.750
All of these things are
going against women,

00:24:30.750 --> 00:24:31.920
biological women,

00:24:31.920 --> 00:24:34.560
when trans women start
to enter their spaces,

00:24:34.560 --> 00:24:36.657
their sports, and compete against them.

00:24:36.657 --> 00:24:38.460
And this is really concerning for me.

00:24:38.460 --> 00:24:41.340
- I think for me it's
not a question of whether

00:24:41.340 --> 00:24:43.230
or not trans women can compete in sports.

00:24:43.230 --> 00:24:48.230
It's a question of how can
we change the institution

00:24:48.630 --> 00:24:51.480
of sports in this country
to make it equitable

00:24:51.480 --> 00:24:53.460
and to create more opportunity

00:24:53.460 --> 00:24:54.540
for cis women--

00:24:54.540 --> 00:24:55.779
- People need to start showing up.

00:24:55.779 --> 00:24:56.612
- For trans women.

00:24:56.612 --> 00:24:58.590
that's kind of like why I wanted
to actually ask y'all like,

00:24:58.590 --> 00:25:00.960
what is your relationship to sports been?

00:25:00.960 --> 00:25:03.000
- I don't think you have to
have a direct relationship

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:04.380
to sports to realize that women

00:25:04.380 --> 00:25:05.910
are being affected by this issue.

00:25:05.910 --> 00:25:08.970
And I do reject the idea of equity.

00:25:08.970 --> 00:25:13.110
There is no way to come
about an equality of outcome,

00:25:13.110 --> 00:25:14.730
which is what equity is saying.

00:25:14.730 --> 00:25:16.980
There's a reason that women's sports

00:25:16.980 --> 00:25:19.710
are less funded and less
watched than men's sports,

00:25:19.710 --> 00:25:22.530
because men seem to excel athletically

00:25:22.530 --> 00:25:23.820
and they seem to press the bounds

00:25:23.820 --> 00:25:26.010
of athleticism way farther than women do.

00:25:26.010 --> 00:25:28.110
We now exist on a slippery slope.

00:25:28.110 --> 00:25:29.610
If it's female sports,

00:25:29.610 --> 00:25:31.290
is it then female locker rooms?

00:25:31.290 --> 00:25:33.180
Is it then female prisons,

00:25:33.180 --> 00:25:36.210
which we're now seeing becoming
an issue here in California

00:25:36.210 --> 00:25:38.160
where biological male inmates

00:25:38.160 --> 00:25:40.050
are being put in female facilities,

00:25:40.050 --> 00:25:42.000
because they identify as women.

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:45.330
We have to discuss as
a society how much we

00:25:45.330 --> 00:25:48.540
give into the feelings of
wanting everybody to be accepted

00:25:48.540 --> 00:25:50.211
and how much we are willing to do that

00:25:50.211 --> 00:25:53.550
at the expense of biological women.

00:25:53.550 --> 00:25:55.800
- I use myself as an example.

00:25:55.800 --> 00:25:58.200
This is about how big I
was in junior high school

00:25:58.200 --> 00:26:00.090
and early high school.

00:26:00.090 --> 00:26:03.840
I used to be able to walk
up to a V8 engine block,

00:26:03.840 --> 00:26:07.014
pick it up off the floor,
and set it on a table.

00:26:07.014 --> 00:26:11.580
And if I was in power
lifting or weightlifting,

00:26:11.580 --> 00:26:12.975
that amount of,

00:26:12.975 --> 00:26:15.780
I mean that advantage
was just unbelievable.

00:26:15.780 --> 00:26:18.150
I've been on hormones for 15 years.

00:26:18.150 --> 00:26:19.230
Did it weaken me?

00:26:19.230 --> 00:26:20.430
Absolutely.

00:26:20.430 --> 00:26:21.750
Did my, you know,

00:26:21.750 --> 00:26:23.580
my bone density really hasn't changed.

00:26:23.580 --> 00:26:25.950
My muscle muscular hasn't changed.

00:26:25.950 --> 00:26:27.780
And this is not a binary question.

00:26:27.780 --> 00:26:29.820
There's a lot of nuances involved.

00:26:29.820 --> 00:26:31.290
- I just want to ask a question

00:26:31.290 --> 00:26:32.820
for what you were saying.

00:26:32.820 --> 00:26:34.803
Can you throw out some statistics?

00:26:36.270 --> 00:26:38.460
- I don't think you need
to have there, so there's,

00:26:38.460 --> 00:26:40.020
there's an abundance of research.

00:26:40.020 --> 00:26:41.730
There's even trans activists who agree

00:26:41.730 --> 00:26:43.140
with exactly what I'm saying.

00:26:43.140 --> 00:26:45.270
And your hormones can change, right?

00:26:45.270 --> 00:26:47.430
And even she just spoke to the fact

00:26:47.430 --> 00:26:49.470
that her bone density did not change .

00:26:49.470 --> 00:26:50.303
- Yeah.

00:26:50.303 --> 00:26:52.002
- In going on hormones
and changing these things.

00:26:52.002 --> 00:26:52.835
- Yeah.

00:26:52.835 --> 00:26:55.080
- And we can see it in sports
as we're watching them.

00:26:55.080 --> 00:26:56.790
Leah Thomas is a great example.

00:26:56.790 --> 00:26:58.950
- So if you can't throw
out the statistics,

00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:00.677
we're not doing enough of the work.

00:27:00.677 --> 00:27:01.954
And let's also be clear--
- I disagree.

00:27:01.954 --> 00:27:02.790
- Let's also be clear,

00:27:02.790 --> 00:27:04.500
there are some cisgender women

00:27:04.500 --> 00:27:07.680
who produce high levels
of testosterone as well.

00:27:07.680 --> 00:27:10.410
And so we really have to unpack it

00:27:10.410 --> 00:27:12.390
from all different sides here.

00:27:12.390 --> 00:27:14.130
- Can you produce statistics

00:27:14.130 --> 00:27:16.290
about the bone density of biological men

00:27:16.290 --> 00:27:18.480
and how it changes upon being on hormones

00:27:18.480 --> 00:27:21.630
and whether or not it levels
out to biological women?

00:27:21.630 --> 00:27:23.430
- I actually cannot because when I would

00:27:23.430 --> 00:27:24.660
think of those statistics,

00:27:24.660 --> 00:27:26.940
I would think it was BS to
be quite honest with you,

00:27:26.940 --> 00:27:29.250
because the reality of it is we could talk

00:27:29.250 --> 00:27:31.920
about statistics and the
research all day long,

00:27:31.920 --> 00:27:33.390
but it's about experience.

00:27:33.390 --> 00:27:35.400
We're gonna be looking
more at the experience,

00:27:35.400 --> 00:27:38.190
because again, when we
look at cisgender women

00:27:38.190 --> 00:27:40.590
who produce high levels of testosterone,

00:27:40.590 --> 00:27:43.112
and who have been kicked out of sports

00:27:43.112 --> 00:27:44.850
and been disqualified

00:27:44.850 --> 00:27:46.740
from teams based on something

00:27:46.740 --> 00:27:50.040
that they biologically cannot control,

00:27:50.040 --> 00:27:52.410
then what are we really
talking about here?

00:27:52.410 --> 00:27:53.400
- Well, we're talking about,

00:27:53.400 --> 00:27:55.980
I mean data and that is overwhelming.

00:27:55.980 --> 00:27:57.570
And we're talking about what is also,

00:27:57.570 --> 00:28:00.150
we're capable of seeing
with our human eyes.

00:28:00.150 --> 00:28:02.550
I think it's very clear
that if you compare

00:28:02.550 --> 00:28:04.170
maybe you to the rest of us,

00:28:04.170 --> 00:28:05.880
there is going to be
a strength difference.

00:28:05.880 --> 00:28:07.202
There's going to be a
bone density difference.

00:28:07.202 --> 00:28:08.035
- You don't know that.

00:28:08.035 --> 00:28:09.930
But you're just saying
that you don't know until

00:28:09.930 --> 00:28:11.910
can we physically do something

00:28:11.910 --> 00:28:14.070
and just perceiving and assuming,

00:28:14.070 --> 00:28:16.020
just because I look a certain way,

00:28:16.020 --> 00:28:17.220
that's not fair.

00:28:17.220 --> 00:28:18.450
Me and her could look the,

00:28:18.450 --> 00:28:20.700
we could look completely
different or whatever,

00:28:20.700 --> 00:28:22.140
but she may be stronger than me.

00:28:22.140 --> 00:28:22.973
- I agree, but we know--

00:28:22.973 --> 00:28:23.806
- She may have,

00:28:23.806 --> 00:28:26.700
she have much more agility
and vitality than I do.

00:28:26.700 --> 00:28:30.027
We don't know that until
you actually do it.

00:28:30.027 --> 00:28:31.826
(talking over each other)

00:28:31.826 --> 00:28:32.991
- And it's been done. We've
seen it numerous times.

00:28:32.991 --> 00:28:35.127
- It's an assumption.

00:28:35.127 --> 00:28:37.973
But we're only going on
assumption at this point,

00:28:37.973 --> 00:28:38.854
because again--

00:28:38.854 --> 00:28:40.920
- It's not assumption when we see,

00:28:40.920 --> 00:28:42.120
when we see it,

00:28:42.120 --> 00:28:44.190
maybe it's the news cycle that I watch,

00:28:44.190 --> 00:28:45.270
but I see it a lot,

00:28:45.270 --> 00:28:47.130
I see it quite often where they're

00:28:47.130 --> 00:28:51.552
showing trans women beating,
I mean, them by far.

00:28:51.552 --> 00:28:53.439
- And you don't see women dominating

00:28:53.439 --> 00:28:55.470
in the men's sports, right?

00:28:55.470 --> 00:28:58.470
You don't see trans men
going into men's sport

00:28:58.470 --> 00:28:59.850
and just completely dominating

00:28:59.850 --> 00:29:01.050
and wiping the field with them.

00:29:01.050 --> 00:29:03.870
This is what happens
when you, in my opinion,

00:29:03.870 --> 00:29:05.340
twist God's design.

00:29:05.340 --> 00:29:06.870
And when you go against God's design,

00:29:06.870 --> 00:29:08.773
you create these problems
that you wouldn't have

00:29:08.773 --> 00:29:12.390
if you weren't going
against what God intended.

00:29:12.390 --> 00:29:14.190
- I'm gonna take her
side a little bit on that

00:29:14.190 --> 00:29:15.360
and let me say one more thing

00:29:15.360 --> 00:29:16.920
and I'm supporting you on this one.

00:29:16.920 --> 00:29:20.550
There are, I mean there's
a great deal of women that,

00:29:20.550 --> 00:29:22.500
and actually there was a
lady in the last Olympics

00:29:22.500 --> 00:29:24.510
that they actually disqualified

00:29:24.510 --> 00:29:27.612
until she went on androgen blockers

00:29:27.612 --> 00:29:31.620
to knock her testosterone
down to a female level.

00:29:31.620 --> 00:29:35.160
Like I said, this is not a
a binary yes or no question.

00:29:35.160 --> 00:29:37.890
And the whole idea of
messing with what you know,

00:29:37.890 --> 00:29:39.780
God puts up, you know,

00:29:39.780 --> 00:29:40.890
God put me up.

00:29:40.890 --> 00:29:43.620
Okay, if you want to take that, you know,

00:29:43.620 --> 00:29:46.800
and I had this conversation
with a very religious man

00:29:46.800 --> 00:29:48.900
in San Diego and he was like,

00:29:48.900 --> 00:29:51.390
oh, I don't quite know
how to deal with that.

00:29:51.390 --> 00:29:52.860
- And God made you that way,

00:29:52.860 --> 00:29:55.364
but he didn't make a lot of
the people transitioning.

00:29:55.364 --> 00:29:56.197
- I understand.

00:29:56.197 --> 00:29:58.500
- But God also understands my transition.

00:29:58.500 --> 00:30:01.500
God, first of all knew what
I was gonna be in my life.

00:30:01.500 --> 00:30:03.240
God already knew I was gonna be trans

00:30:03.240 --> 00:30:04.710
when God put me here.

00:30:04.710 --> 00:30:05.698
- So, why didn't he--

00:30:05.698 --> 00:30:08.550
- I don't think it's fair
when people dip and dab.

00:30:08.550 --> 00:30:10.343
Your relationship with God is personal.

00:30:10.343 --> 00:30:11.730
- Yes.
- It's sacred.

00:30:11.730 --> 00:30:12.563
- Let's keep it there.

00:30:12.563 --> 00:30:14.280
- I don't think it's fair
when other people dip and dab

00:30:14.280 --> 00:30:16.200
and other people's relationship with God

00:30:16.200 --> 00:30:17.580
when they don't understand
what they go through.

00:30:17.580 --> 00:30:20.220
God still blesses me as a trans woman.

00:30:20.220 --> 00:30:22.320
God blesses you as a cisgendered woman.

00:30:22.320 --> 00:30:27.060
God is embodied in me as a trans person.

00:30:27.060 --> 00:30:28.320
I don't think it's fair.

00:30:28.320 --> 00:30:32.610
Again, when we judge people's
personal relationship

00:30:32.610 --> 00:30:35.820
with God, gender identity,
sexual orientation,

00:30:35.820 --> 00:30:39.570
none of that matters to
a God that loves all.

00:30:39.570 --> 00:30:41.733
- [Narrator] Gender dysphoria is real.

00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:47.130
- I think it is obviously real,

00:30:47.130 --> 00:30:49.200
because many people experience it.

00:30:49.200 --> 00:30:51.600
But like any kind of dysphoria,

00:30:51.600 --> 00:30:54.630
whether it's someone who
thinks they're overweight

00:30:54.630 --> 00:30:57.840
or anything, I think it should
be treated as not reality.

00:30:57.840 --> 00:31:00.150
Like if I thought I was obese,

00:31:00.150 --> 00:31:02.910
I wouldn't want to go
to a affirming therapist

00:31:02.910 --> 00:31:04.710
to tell me, yes, you are
obese and you should,

00:31:04.710 --> 00:31:06.420
you know, get skinnier.

00:31:06.420 --> 00:31:09.840
- Well, I had the opportunity
of working on the DSM4,

00:31:09.840 --> 00:31:11.340
I think it was when we,

00:31:11.340 --> 00:31:16.080
when we actually declassified
transgender dysphoria

00:31:16.080 --> 00:31:18.360
from a mental illness to a condition.

00:31:18.360 --> 00:31:20.130
You know, I had been,
at that point in time,

00:31:20.130 --> 00:31:24.660
I had been cross-dressing
for 50 years and you know,

00:31:24.660 --> 00:31:29.660
because that dysphoria was
there and every single thing I

00:31:30.270 --> 00:31:32.670
did to try to drive it away didn't work.

00:31:32.670 --> 00:31:35.861
I spent millions of dollars trying to

00:31:35.861 --> 00:31:38.587
be the coolest dude in the world.

00:31:38.587 --> 00:31:40.800
You know, I bought airplanes,

00:31:40.800 --> 00:31:44.220
I bought everything that I
could to just show the world

00:31:44.220 --> 00:31:45.450
how masculine I was.

00:31:45.450 --> 00:31:46.830
It didn't work,

00:31:46.830 --> 00:31:47.970
it didn't go away.

00:31:47.970 --> 00:31:49.683
And I did therapy.

00:31:49.683 --> 00:31:52.920
I purposely went to a therapist that

00:31:52.920 --> 00:31:57.920
was anti gender affirming
and literally he said,

00:31:59.236 --> 00:32:01.890
"You need to do this."

00:32:01.890 --> 00:32:05.310
You know, and because
it was so deep seeded.

00:32:05.310 --> 00:32:08.730
Spent six weeks as Gina with my son.

00:32:08.730 --> 00:32:10.980
And at the end of that period of time

00:32:10.980 --> 00:32:13.470
he asked two very fundamental questions.

00:32:13.470 --> 00:32:15.840
The most important one was,

00:32:15.840 --> 00:32:20.190
it's gotta be truly exhausting
for you to lead two lives.

00:32:20.190 --> 00:32:21.240
And I was kinda like,

00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:22.620
that kind of shook me to the core

00:32:22.620 --> 00:32:27.030
that my 22 year old son
saw that better than I did.

00:32:27.030 --> 00:32:28.680
So shortly thereafter,

00:32:28.680 --> 00:32:33.600
I announced to my family
that I was gonna transition.

00:32:33.600 --> 00:32:35.970
My wife and I separated because of it.

00:32:35.970 --> 00:32:40.609
The kids were not necessarily shocked,

00:32:40.609 --> 00:32:42.450
but you know, understood,

00:32:42.450 --> 00:32:44.910
and have supported me quite well.

00:32:44.910 --> 00:32:48.210
And my wife has actually
become a very good,

00:32:48.210 --> 00:32:51.360
you know, very warm
supporting person for me.

00:32:51.360 --> 00:32:54.330
- Gender dysphoria almost
made me kill myself.

00:32:54.330 --> 00:32:56.760
And coming from Mississippi at the time,

00:32:56.760 --> 00:32:58.050
there wasn't a lot of access

00:32:58.050 --> 00:33:01.590
to gender affirming
resources, like hormones,

00:33:01.590 --> 00:33:03.270
if I wanted surgery,,

00:33:03.270 --> 00:33:04.830
whatever the case may be.

00:33:04.830 --> 00:33:06.690
And a lot of us trans folks who don't

00:33:06.690 --> 00:33:08.130
have access like that,

00:33:08.130 --> 00:33:10.410
a lot of us have to do sex work to be able

00:33:10.410 --> 00:33:12.420
to afford some of these things as well.

00:33:12.420 --> 00:33:14.580
Me coming up at the age of 20

00:33:14.580 --> 00:33:16.530
and I knew I had a
serious gender dysphoria.

00:33:16.530 --> 00:33:20.400
I did things to my body that I should

00:33:20.400 --> 00:33:21.990
have went to a hospital to do.

00:33:21.990 --> 00:33:24.750
That is something that's very, very hard

00:33:24.750 --> 00:33:25.800
for people to understand.

00:33:25.800 --> 00:33:27.720
A lot of us commit suicide,

00:33:27.720 --> 00:33:29.100
because of gender dysphoria

00:33:29.100 --> 00:33:31.320
and so it hits our community a lot harder.

00:33:31.320 --> 00:33:34.620
- I do think gender
dysphoria is very much real.

00:33:34.620 --> 00:33:36.210
I think the issue that's happened,

00:33:36.210 --> 00:33:38.430
especially in the space
of science and research

00:33:38.430 --> 00:33:40.110
is that we've looked at gender dysphoria

00:33:40.110 --> 00:33:43.200
and said the only source of
care that we can go through

00:33:43.200 --> 00:33:45.930
is blind gender affirmation care.

00:33:45.930 --> 00:33:47.730
And a lot of the research shows that this

00:33:47.730 --> 00:33:49.350
is not the route to go into.

00:33:49.350 --> 00:33:50.850
And other countries that have decided

00:33:50.850 --> 00:33:54.300
to do nonpartisan
research, Sweden, Finland,

00:33:54.300 --> 00:33:56.490
have decided that yes,

00:33:56.490 --> 00:33:59.160
gender affirmation care
should be an option,

00:33:59.160 --> 00:34:01.020
but it really should be the last resort

00:34:01.020 --> 00:34:03.510
when it comes to treating
people who appear

00:34:03.510 --> 00:34:05.651
at clinics with gender dysphoria.

00:34:05.651 --> 00:34:07.500
You know, a lot of
conservatives will deny and say,

00:34:07.500 --> 00:34:10.140
well, gender affirmation care
does not make them happier.

00:34:10.140 --> 00:34:12.000
And in many cases that is true.

00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:13.890
But there are the cases
like your yourselves

00:34:13.890 --> 00:34:16.830
where the gender affirmation
care does make them happier.

00:34:16.830 --> 00:34:17.970
- You know, I know a lot of people

00:34:17.970 --> 00:34:21.825
that have transitioned,
have un-transitioned.

00:34:21.825 --> 00:34:23.373
I've talked with a gentleman

00:34:23.373 --> 00:34:27.240
at a religious right convention one day

00:34:27.240 --> 00:34:30.030
and he was sitting there
screaming how Jesus

00:34:30.030 --> 00:34:32.940
got him out of his gender transition.

00:34:32.940 --> 00:34:36.030
And honestly, that was
the saddest man I've ever

00:34:36.030 --> 00:34:37.650
talked to in my life.

00:34:37.650 --> 00:34:39.420
When I looked at him straight in the eyes,

00:34:39.420 --> 00:34:43.380
and I said, "You know, hey, I
don't agree with what you say,

00:34:43.380 --> 00:34:46.680
but I 100% support your
right to say that."

00:34:46.680 --> 00:34:49.410
And he just literally broke down crying

00:34:49.410 --> 00:34:50.970
on the steps of the Supreme Court.

00:34:50.970 --> 00:34:52.860
- If I could interject
really quickly, I do--

00:34:52.860 --> 00:34:54.286
- No, absolutely not.

00:34:54.286 --> 00:34:56.520
- I feel as though the medical profession

00:34:56.520 --> 00:34:58.500
is actually inching towards a space

00:34:58.500 --> 00:35:00.300
that is going to become unsafe for people

00:35:00.300 --> 00:35:02.280
who try to express their gender dysphoria.

00:35:02.280 --> 00:35:04.140
Because now we have young children

00:35:04.140 --> 00:35:05.910
coming into clinics expressing this,

00:35:05.910 --> 00:35:06.743
who by and large,

00:35:06.743 --> 00:35:10.650
statistically about 60 to 70%
grow out of that dysphoria.

00:35:10.650 --> 00:35:12.660
But because it's become a political issue,

00:35:12.660 --> 00:35:15.270
where many activists
have come in and say no,

00:35:15.270 --> 00:35:16.770
you blindly affirm,

00:35:16.770 --> 00:35:19.890
you affirm to to the
furthest extent that you can.

00:35:19.890 --> 00:35:22.680
Rather than going through a
more comprehensive process

00:35:22.680 --> 00:35:23.760
with these children,

00:35:23.760 --> 00:35:26.910
we have a, what I think is
a medical tragedy happening

00:35:26.910 --> 00:35:29.250
against young people in this country.

00:35:29.250 --> 00:35:31.473
- [Narrator] I have
been sexually harassed.

00:35:39.630 --> 00:35:43.020
- Yeah, I think in our society
it's so sexualized every,

00:35:43.020 --> 00:35:44.250
everyone and everything.

00:35:44.250 --> 00:35:46.890
And I think we owe a lot
of that to pornography

00:35:46.890 --> 00:35:48.240
and just media.

00:35:48.240 --> 00:35:50.460
And I think the kind of acceptance

00:35:50.460 --> 00:35:53.874
that I do see more so in
the LGBT community of like,

00:35:53.874 --> 00:35:57.630
you know, sex is great
and let like everyone talk

00:35:57.630 --> 00:35:58.800
about it and there's no shame

00:35:58.800 --> 00:36:00.600
and everyone's just blurting out.

00:36:00.600 --> 00:36:03.674
You know, the fact that
we're perpetuating a culture

00:36:03.674 --> 00:36:06.780
that's frankly, in my opinion, disgusting.

00:36:06.780 --> 00:36:10.140
- So, are you talking
specifically about LGBT people?

00:36:10.140 --> 00:36:13.440
- I'm talking more so just
about this sexual revolution

00:36:13.440 --> 00:36:14.730
that the more sexual you are,

00:36:14.730 --> 00:36:15.750
the more partners you have,

00:36:15.750 --> 00:36:18.210
the more open you are about
your sex life and everything,

00:36:18.210 --> 00:36:20.610
the more like liberated you are.

00:36:20.610 --> 00:36:21.601
What is consent?

00:36:21.601 --> 00:36:24.699
Like people are coming
outta the woodwork saying,

00:36:24.699 --> 00:36:25.590
you know, I was violated,

00:36:25.590 --> 00:36:26.940
this happened to me and,

00:36:26.940 --> 00:36:29.370
but they like drove home with that person.

00:36:29.370 --> 00:36:30.439
And I'm not blaming them,

00:36:30.439 --> 00:36:33.000
but I am saying those
lines are being blurred,

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:36.720
because of our just flagrant
disregard for any kind

00:36:36.720 --> 00:36:41.580
of like actual relationship
prior to the sexual encounter.

00:36:41.580 --> 00:36:42.600
And I think a lot of people

00:36:42.600 --> 00:36:44.400
are being exploited left and right.

00:36:44.400 --> 00:36:46.380
- True sex positivity has been powerful.

00:36:46.380 --> 00:36:50.130
It has helped us to grow
and learn about our bodies

00:36:50.130 --> 00:36:52.770
in so many ways and
learn safe sex practices

00:36:52.770 --> 00:36:54.150
in so many ways.

00:36:54.150 --> 00:36:57.060
What I would blame for rape culture

00:36:57.060 --> 00:36:59.160
or for a lack of good boundaries

00:36:59.160 --> 00:37:02.580
or that kind of thing is we
live in a capitalist system

00:37:02.580 --> 00:37:06.634
that has taken things like sex positivity

00:37:06.634 --> 00:37:09.360
and mangled it and repackaged it

00:37:09.360 --> 00:37:12.762
and made it a whole other
thing than what it actually is.

00:37:12.762 --> 00:37:16.920
- I was sexually harassed
for five years by a woman.

00:37:16.920 --> 00:37:17.850
That does happen,

00:37:17.850 --> 00:37:19.230
'cause I'm pretty sure it's gonna be

00:37:19.230 --> 00:37:20.250
where men this men that,

00:37:20.250 --> 00:37:22.800
it's hard coming from a man,

00:37:22.800 --> 00:37:24.527
but to me it was harder
coming from a woman,

00:37:24.527 --> 00:37:26.280
'cause it wasn't expected.

00:37:26.280 --> 00:37:29.550
Like I understand, you're
gonna probably touch on that

00:37:29.550 --> 00:37:32.880
about how men are more
on the predatory side

00:37:32.880 --> 00:37:35.760
or the more harassing side sometimes.

00:37:35.760 --> 00:37:36.903
But I just wanna let let you know

00:37:36.903 --> 00:37:38.853
that it does happen with women as well.

00:37:41.550 --> 00:37:43.170
- All through my life, you know,

00:37:43.170 --> 00:37:45.030
world's biggest kid in junior high school,

00:37:45.030 --> 00:37:47.962
I basically was harassed continuously

00:37:47.962 --> 00:37:50.700
for being gender nonconforming.

00:37:50.700 --> 00:37:52.770
Back then, you know, everybody
in junior high school

00:37:52.770 --> 00:37:53.760
took showers together.

00:37:53.760 --> 00:37:56.586
I basically had a
permanent welt on my bottom

00:37:56.586 --> 00:37:58.987
from people snapping towels at me because,

00:37:58.987 --> 00:38:01.980
you know, I wasn't as well
endowed as I probably should be.

00:38:01.980 --> 00:38:04.230
I had, you know, pretty
good size boy boobs

00:38:04.230 --> 00:38:07.320
and basically was just
unhappy being in sports.

00:38:07.320 --> 00:38:10.560
But you know, it happens everywhere.

00:38:10.560 --> 00:38:12.874
I have been sexually assaulted,

00:38:12.874 --> 00:38:17.160
and it didn't work out
well for any of them.

00:38:17.160 --> 00:38:18.960
It's real, let me just put it that way.

00:38:18.960 --> 00:38:20.430
It's absolutely real.

00:38:20.430 --> 00:38:21.870
- Yeah. I think it'd be
hard to find a person

00:38:21.870 --> 00:38:23.970
who hasn't been sexually harassed

00:38:23.970 --> 00:38:25.020
in some way, shape, or form,

00:38:25.020 --> 00:38:26.520
whether you are male or female.

00:38:26.520 --> 00:38:28.650
I think it's an experience
that we all share,

00:38:28.650 --> 00:38:32.010
because we are in somewhat
of a hypersexualized society

00:38:32.010 --> 00:38:34.800
and people love to make
those comments public.

00:38:34.800 --> 00:38:38.340
I am a podcaster and I do
social media for a living.

00:38:38.340 --> 00:38:39.270
So as you can imagine,

00:38:39.270 --> 00:38:42.780
the onslaught of sexual
harassment is quite, quite vast.

00:38:42.780 --> 00:38:44.553
- From a very young age,

00:38:45.900 --> 00:38:48.360
I've had this recurring nightmare

00:38:48.360 --> 00:38:51.570
of something happening to me,

00:38:51.570 --> 00:38:54.303
trying to warn people
and no one believes me.

00:38:55.650 --> 00:38:59.667
When you're not believed that
you are a desirable person,

00:38:59.667 --> 00:39:01.131
and I really don't think rape has anything

00:39:01.131 --> 00:39:02.340
to do with desire,

00:39:02.340 --> 00:39:04.230
but when you're not believed in that way,

00:39:04.230 --> 00:39:07.380
when trans women are
experiencing trans misogyny,

00:39:07.380 --> 00:39:09.330
we are the ones who are least believed

00:39:09.330 --> 00:39:11.433
when we are sexually assaulted.

00:39:13.170 --> 00:39:17.834
And it just feels so
disempowering and so terrifying

00:39:17.834 --> 00:39:20.280
when you know that you are someone

00:39:20.280 --> 00:39:22.710
who is seen as hypersexual,

00:39:22.710 --> 00:39:26.160
as inherently sexual,
as inherently predatory.

00:39:26.160 --> 00:39:30.153
And yet at the same time
you're seen as someone who,

00:39:32.280 --> 00:39:35.940
can be isolated and sexually
assaulted and not believed.

00:39:35.940 --> 00:39:38.190
- I don't think there's
anything inherently predatory

00:39:38.190 --> 00:39:39.270
about trans people.

00:39:39.270 --> 00:39:41.970
And I think oftentimes when we are talking

00:39:41.970 --> 00:39:43.290
from a conservative perspective,

00:39:43.290 --> 00:39:45.990
it gets misconstrued as
viewing you as a threat.

00:39:45.990 --> 00:39:48.270
And I hope that that never comes off.

00:39:48.270 --> 00:39:50.880
And I think that allegations
of sexual assault,

00:39:50.880 --> 00:39:52.380
regardless of who they're coming from,

00:39:52.380 --> 00:39:53.763
should be taken seriously.

00:39:57.570 --> 00:39:58.403
- Common ground.

00:39:58.403 --> 00:39:59.659
. I think we agreed on something.

00:39:59.659 --> 00:40:00.527
- Found common ground.

00:40:00.527 --> 00:40:01.360
(laughing)

00:40:01.360 --> 00:40:04.027
(intense music)

00:40:19.990 --> 00:40:21.118
(music ending)

